From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: mm8013: report the current with the documented sign

The power supply ABI says that current_now is negative while a battery
discharges and positive while it charges. This driver negates the
register and reports the opposite.

On a Lenovo TB375FC charging from a USB port, with status reading
Charging, current_now stays between -376000 and -488000 while charge_now
rises by 515 mAh in 4011 seconds, or 462 mA, and capacity goes from 19
to 25.

UPower takes a negative current_now for a battery that discharges,
whatever status says, unless the battery is full. Desktops built on it
then show this battery as discharging all the time it charges, with the
time left until it is empty.

The register needs no change of sign. CURRENT_MAX keeps its negation:
that register holds the largest load as a negative number, and the
result reads 4784000 on the same device.

With this change the same device reads 510000 with status Charging and
-585000 with status Discharging.

---
diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/mm8013.c b/drivers/power/supply/mm8013.c
--- a/drivers/power/supply/mm8013.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/mm8013.c
@@ -147,7 +147,7 @@
 		if (ret < 0)
 			return ret;
 
-		val->intval = -1000 * (s16)regval;
+		val->intval = 1000 * (s16)regval;
 		break;
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CYCLE_COUNT:
 		ret = regmap_read(chip->regmap, REG_CYCLE_COUNT, &regval);
